{"kind":"artifact","text":"Minimal user documentation set on branch task/docs, unmerged. docs/getting-started.md is one ordered path — install, initialize, join over MCP, work through request/promise/report/ratify, verify, audit from a fresh clone — with every command executed against a throwaway repository rather than transcribed. docs/reference.md carries the command tables, event identifier form, MCP tools and protocol era, and the one-service-per-repository and ready-banner constraints. The root README keeps the argument and the build and delegates the rest, which removes the duplication instead of relocating it. Repaired five links the rearrangement broke: three in the README pointing at the pre-move design note, bootstrap plan, and demos, and two inside the moved notes still addressing SKILL.md as though at the root. Testing the documented commands corrected three claims: gs state prints the bare event identifier on stdout; ratify and supersede take a positional target and flag parsing stops there, so flags must precede the event, which the first reference draft had backwards and which does not run; and superseding a request does propagate staleness to an artifact resting on it, observed rather than assumed. The MCP section states plainly that this build serves only the stateless 2026-07-28 shape and that clients opening with initialize cannot attach, because the walkthrough would otherwise lie at its third step. Validated: 29 relative links and anchors across 19 markdown files resolve; make vet, make test, make build pass; make ui rebuilds byte-identical output. Not reviewed and not merged; this cites the branch head only.","body":{"commit":"420efecd2cc7dd4324526083493df477b2544e94","path":"."}}